<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  :feature:notification copy.

  WORDING RULES that apply to every string in this file, not only to the ones already here:
  no claim about removing viruses, blocking scams, speeding a phone up or freeing memory, and no
  performance percentage figures. A measured number is reported with its unit; what the number will
  do for the user is never asserted. The competitor's equivalents of these screens are where that
  copy concentrates.

  Every string is resolved with `stringResource` at render, never held on a model. `ae.i2` resolves
  feature names to Strings from `Resources` at object initialisation, in an app with a 17-locale
  in-app picker, so switching language leaves them stale until the process restarts
  (`docs/system-architecture.md` §4.3).
-->
